  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_37c299d258d84c62ac2fb3e984e7c326",
      "statement": "HAAP's rate limiter (haap/rate_limiter.py) is a token-bucket abuse control that bounds message-driven cost: every checked message consumes one token from the per-(friend, action) bucket and one from the friend's global '*' bucket, and when either bucket is empty the message is rejected. RateLimiter.check() returns True only if both takes succeed, returns False instead of raising when raise_on_limit=False, and otherwise raises RateLimitedError with a retry_after hint.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://haap/rate_limiter.py#L1-L12",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:87d343e2b553d1f27e5b9f7af84cd06f7ed2d7a326d634a3a153511c1d2cb7a8:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://haap/rate_limiter.py#L109-L131",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:60a8cd863187af658856f65e3a643a87a94665528efd043d20a6b60ed851de49:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_8d777f14a14c4b5aaedb7cf766813b5a",
      "statement": "Each token bucket (haap/rate_limiter.py _Bucket) holds a burst capacity plus a continuous per-second refill; buckets start full (tokens == capacity), refill lazily on access to at most capacity, and take() requires at least 1.0 token and removes exactly one. A zero refill_per_sec disables refill and wait_seconds() returns infinity.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://haap/rate_limiter.py#L35-L65",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:cc4b96338d84c1d4c09cc8cec720c5b1c93773cce946dc61de49daccafde875c:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_5b58af81d94a4784aed423db2b6e66d8",
      "statement": "Rate limiter state is process-local and deliberately not persisted: token math is serialized by the process-wide class lock RateLimiter._GLOBAL_LOCK inside _Bucket.take, a per-instance lock guards the bucket dictionary, buckets are created lazily on first check, and the whole set is rebuilt full on restart. RateLimiter.reset() clears one fingerprint's buckets or all of them and configure() pre-creates a bucket; neither is called by the server or client today.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://haap/rate_limiter.py#L100-L107",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:68ad971ab63cc4a97d442845e5d38632641ac3bbf3624dde3ab7bca23f3d43de:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://haap/rate_limiter.py#L133-L139",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:36d304696024310adde1f8f4a0d92dc21c7b1ece56470c90f1d20b07e8d3f94a:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://haap/rate_limiter.py#L52-L77",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:2a25348a4ccf35eb8d0c19b8db482e7d4084979c866230f97db502b7af299ba0:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_3a114102eadb46c8a9c4812c26d897e2",
      "statement": "Per-friend rate limits are durable configuration stored as FriendRecord.rate_limits (an action-keyed map of {action: {capacity, refill_per_sec}}) inside friends.json, stamped at approval time by Directory.approve(rate_limits=...); at runtime config_for() resolves a friend's limits per action and per field with fallback order: friend's own entry, then the RateLimiter default catalog entry, then the catalog's '*' global entry.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://haap/directory.py#L273-L286",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:1ad92010a5d90f8d0564c16e13a37efaaef9acf13e6c371bcd3d68f8ed8eb2f4:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://haap/directory.py#L58-L86",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:3cbb4038be135be06575a5550e99d0ae2e4564425da4528c312be172f81a1878:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://haap/rate_limiter.py#L88-L97",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:35afd3f8adb93de21a19ca28a8477dc14ae8c753f1826febb120ef2f37eaa1f2:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_7900c8ef6ef94e0eabf494e10c922f53",
      "statement": "The shipped default catalog rate_limiter.DEFAULT_CATALOG applies when a friend configures no limit: global '*' capacity 60 refill 0.5/s, task_request 5/0.05, task_result 10/0.1, task_progress 20/0.2, chat:converse 20/0.2, hello 10/0.1, friend_request 3/0.02, verify 10/0.1, error 10/0.1; directory.DEFAULT_RATE_LIMITS is an illustrative subset copy of the same idea.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://haap/directory.py#L44-L51",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:611b65e5e38e1a08cb938d0156a64c15c3abe790e107ab4955347116275833c2:"
        },
        {
