    },
    {
      "id": "claim_e08b7f60aca748d4897abf4a143b6588",
      "statement": "The reference enforcement point is the inbound task_request handler (server.py::_on_task_request): after the sender must be an accepted friend and the payload action/resource must pass the permission matrix, rate_limiter.check(sender, action, rec.rate_limits) runs before the task is created and the executor invoked — so a permission-denied task_request never reaches the model and never consumes a token bucket (denial-of-wallet defense T8).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://haap/server.py#L283-L295",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b742568e7ccdbc54c40b28b3e3d5d8d5e6940a06ec490871c7617bd241743d7f:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_beb2b339b97c4cde82e2d50ca9d55ec2",
      "statement": "Marketplace open-service traffic (service_search, service_book, service_cancel) is gated by server._check_marketplace_sender with a dedicated stricter inline catalog — a 'marketplace' bucket of capacity 10 refill 0.05/s plus a global of 20 refill 0.1/s — and a blocked sender fingerprint is rejected with PERMISSION_DENIED before the rate-limit check runs.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://haap/server.py#L337-L350",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:0db5512ed44780d2d5691ee96195ac8ef0dd448d89506222a7227ab2fcb0d664:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_18bc29de6f7c4373bb0b755b31246880",
      "statement": "The client mirrors the guard outbound: client.py::_send checks the friend is accepted and the action passes the local permission matrix, then calls rate_limiter.check(self.identity.fingerprint, 'task:submit') with no friend limits (so the default catalog applies) before the envelope leaves the machine — an outbound self-throttle keyed on the local identity fingerprint.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://haap/client.py#L95-L117",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6dc2dd18304970b40045ea0e1a30741244cf8b6e51cf43ecbc0252aa295df72c:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_c33603592ec5491e8b8cea10928b4c61",
      "statement": "Only three enforcement points call rate_limiter.check today (inbound task_request, marketplace open services, client outbound task_request): the handshake and housekeeping message types — hello, challenge, friend_request, friend_accept, ping, inbound task_result — are not token-gated even though the default catalog names hello/friend_request/verify/error buckets; pre-friendship flooding is instead bounded by the envelope size cap and nonce/timestamp machinery.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://haap/rate_limiter.py#L21-L32",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:586267fe9b626d89e8046b5e32f2a71a9638f2a9e21d75766cd0b6ca368a8219:"
