    {
      "id": "claim_1f332f9d291843a9acddc80d717f1080",
      "statement": "Focused tests exercise the abuse controls end-to-end through the same router the HTTP layer uses: test_server.py::test_task_rate_limit approves a friend with a capacity-1 task:submit bucket and asserts the second task_request returns an error envelope with error_code RATE_LIMITED; test_marketplace.py::test_marketplace_rate_limit sends 12 service_search messages against the capacity-10 marketplace bucket and asserts requests eventually fail; and every fixture in the test suite attaches AuditLog(memory=True), so all handled messages run the real event/redaction code path.",
